{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-07-16-south-korea-a2/audio/main-1f6c41e344e6.mp3","durationSec":86.904,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.64,"text":"Gwangjang Market is a historic market in Seoul."},{"start":3.5,"end":6.24,"text":"It has food stalls and shops for clothing and fabric."},{"start":6.98,"end":10.68,"text":"Two foods to try are mayak gimbap and nokdujeon."},{"start":10.68,"end":16.42,"text":"Mayak gimbap are small rice rolls, and nokdujeon are savoury pancakes made from mung beans."},{"start":17.5,"end":19.66,"text":"Another important Korean food is kimchi."},{"start":19.66,"end":24.48,"text":"Families and communities make and share kimchi in a tradition called kimjang."},{"start":25.66,"end":30.28,"text":"UNESCO added kimjang to its Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2013."},{"start":32.14,"end":35.22,"text":"Gyeongbokgung was the main royal palace of the Joseon dynasty."},{"start":36,"end":38.02,"text":"It was established in 1395."},{"start":38.82,"end":43.18,"text":"Its name expresses a wish for the new dynasty to enjoy great fortune and prosperity."},{"start":44.26,"end":51.1,"text":"Important cultural work took place there, including work connected to Hunminjeongeum, the original name of the Korean alphabet."},{"start":51.52,"end":56.02,"text":"The palace was destroyed in 1592 and restored in 1867."},{"start":56.5,"end":61.26,"text":"If you travel there, check a current subway map and ask for help when you need it."},{"start":61.26,"end":65.26,"text":"Myeong-dong is a shopping area in central Seoul."},{"start":65.86,"end":67.44,"text":"It is known for fashion and food."},{"start":68.1,"end":71.9,"text":"The area also has Myeong-dong Cathedral and two major department stores."},{"start":72.52,"end":76.3,"text":"You can visit shops, compare clothes, and stop for something to eat."},{"start":76.82,"end":80.56,"text":"When you buy clothes, check the label because size systems can be different."},{"start":81.02,"end":84.08,"text":"If you are not sure, ask, ‘What size is this?’"},{"start":84.08,"end":86.46,"text":"or ‘Can I try this on?’"}],"words":[{"text":"Gwangjang","start":0,"end":0.58},{"text":"Market","start":0.58,"end":1},{"text":"is","start":1,"end":1.28},{"text":"a","start":1.28,"end":1.4},{"text":"historic","start":1.4,"end":1.8},{"text":"market","start":1.8,"end":2.12},{"text":"in","start":2.12,"end":2.36},{"text":"Seoul","start":2.36,"end":2.64},{"text":"It","start":3.5,"end":3.6},{"text":"has","start":3.6,"end":3.78},{"text":"food","start":3.78,"end":4.06},{"text":"stalls","start":4.06,"end":4.38},{"text":"and","start":4.38,"end":4.74},{"text":"shops","start":4.74,"end":5.04},{"text":"for","start":5.04,"end":5.32},{"text":"clothing","start":5.32,"end":5.66},{"text":"and","start":5.66,"end":5.86},{"text":"fabric","start":5.86,"end":6.24},{"text":"Two","start":6.98,"end":7.24},{"text":"foods","start":7.24,"end":7.46},{"text":"to","start":7.46,"end":7.68},{"text":"try","start":7.68,"end":7.96},{"text":"are","start":7.96,"end":8.2},{"text":"mayak","start":8.2,"end":8.58},{"text":"gimbap","start":8.58,"end":9.02},{"text":"and","start":9.02,"end":9.36},{"text":"nokdujeon","start":9.36,"end":10.68},{"text":"Mayak","start":10.68,"end":11.06},{"text":"gimbap","start":11.06,"end":11.58},{"text":"are","start":11.58,"end":11.8},{"text":"small","start":11.8,"end":12.18},{"text":"rice","start":12.18,"end":12.48},{"text":"rolls","start":12.48,"end":12.84},{"text":"and","start":13.32,"end":13.54},{"text":"nokdujeon","start":13.54,"end":14.18},{"text":"are","start":14.18,"end":14.38},{"text":"savoury","start":14.38,"end":14.82},{"text":"pancakes","start":14.82,"end":15.28},{"text":"made","start":15.28,"end":15.66},{"text":"from","start":15.66,"end":15.94},{"text":"mung","start":15.94,"end":16.1},{"text":"beans","start":16.1,"end":16.42},{"text":"Another","start":17.5,"end":17.74},{"text":"important","start":17.74,"end":18.2},{"text":"Korean","start":18.2,"end":18.5},{"text":